{"notes":["Scope reviewed: worktree feat/ts-mcp-feedback-tool commit 6eef2f4 vs base 9a22f69 — 16 files changed (feedback_new/list/publish as MCP write tools). Reviewed: internal/mcp/server.go (Capability + handleToolsList + callTool dispatch), internal/eka/feedback.go (thin capability mirroring CLI), internal/feedback/{model,store,publish,github}.go (ADR-026 engine, file store, token gate, issue client), tests (feedback_test.go, conformance/fuzz/hardening), skills/docs/mcp-boundary.md + README/CHANGELOG/pack.go/anvil.yaml. Threat model: token exfiltration via logs/outputs, path traversal on id, CKO contamination, DoS via large payloads, publish idempotency, error sanitization.","Gates: GOCACHE=/tmp/opencode-marij/go-cache GOTMPDIR=/tmp/opencode-marij go build ./... -\u003e green (exit 0); go vet ./... -\u003e green (no output); go test ./... -\u003e green (eka-mcp 0.14s, cmd/eka-mcp 2.5s, internal/eka 0.77s, internal/mcp 0.91s, internal/feedback no test files). Targeted: go test -run TestFeedback ./internal/eka -v PASS 10/10 (New/CreateDraft/Scaffold/Validation/ListOrdering/PublishUnauth/InvalidToken/Success/UnknownID/NeverBecomesCKO/TokenNotInError).","Finding LOW (process): Ordering deviation noted per task — work item eka/ts:mcp-feedback-tool:1 already transitioned done (in-review-\u003edone 2026-08-25) while implementation note cmt:mcp-feedback-tool-implementation (rev1) is still draft noteState=resolved but contentState=draft with empty {changes:[], summary:'', tests:[]} and draft list reports invalid — 1 error. Implementation note published resolved before work item done is expected; current order is inverted. No code impact, but violates EKA note-state gate (only note-state:resolved releases done gate). Evidence: eka get shows done + history, draft file shows state resolved + invalid marker, eka draft list output. Mitigation: republish implementation note with proper summary/changes/tests or allow deviation as documented; no rework needed for MCP code.","Finding SECURE (pass): 3 tools exactly mirror CLI — feedback_new same validation (type/title required, closed sets type{bug|suggestion|improvement|question} severity{low|medium|high} source{human|agent}), per-type scaffold (bug -\u003e Steps/Expected/Actual else Description), fbk-YYYYMMDD-slug + collision suffix -2/-3, 0700 dir/0600 file via Save; feedback_list deterministic id-descending + first-malformed-fails-whole-list naming file + [] not null; feedback_publish same engine feedback.Publish with pre-flight Load/Validate. Evidence: diff server.go + feedback.go + store.go, feedback_test.go scaffold tests, conformance byte-determinism checks.","Finding SECURE (pass): ADR-026 invariants intact — feedback never enters canonical store, never becomes CKO. Package feedback is standalone (imports only fmt/os/path/filepath/sort/strings/time/unicode, yaml.v3) — no store/workspace/sync import. Store rooted at \u003chome\u003e/feedback (Dir=Join(home,feedback)). MCP descriptions explicitly state never CKO. Evidence: feedback/model.go header 'never a CKO, never a unit', feedback_test TestFeedbackNeverBecomesCKO checks Get/domain don't return feedback, List error path not hitting store.","Finding SECURE (pass): Publish constraints inherited unchanged — release-binary gate: issueToken=='' =\u003e 'issue token not bundled — use a release binary' (publish.go:37-38); tests map to deterministic refusal. Invalid token 401/403 mapped to 'publish failed: invalid token — use a release binary' not raw API (feedback.go:248-250). Token never appears in outputs/errors/logs: IssueClient only sets Authorization: Bearer header, never marshaled; errors sanitized, tests assert no Bearer/token= and no leaked secret (TestFeedbackPublishTokenNotInSanitizedError, conformance unauthenticated check). Fixed target https://api.github.com/repos/maleolabs/eka-cli/issues, var only for tests via SetIssueAPIURL/SetIssueToken. Evidence: github.go + publish.go + feedback.go error mapping + tests.","Finding SECURE (pass): Error sanitization \u0026 path leak prevention — all tool errors go via SanitizeError (first line only, pathRe/relPathRe -\u003e \u003cpath\u003e, no stack). Publish errors mapped to deterministic remediations (token gate, invalid token, network -\u003e 'cannot reach GitHub — check network', unknown id -\u003e 'unknown feedback', already-published -\u003e 'already published as #n \u003curl\u003e'). Store Load validates id: Base(id)!=id or contains /\\ =\u003e 'invalid feedback id'. List malformed file fails naming Base(path). Success path disclosure (path field = \u003chome\u003e/feedback/fbk-...md) is intentional user-scoped, not cross-user leak — errors correctly sanitize. Evidence: server.go SanitizeError + conformance/hardening tests (TestSanitizeError, TestToolErrorNoInternalLeakage, TestFeedbackPublishUnknownID path checks).","Finding LOW (informational): Minor hardening edge — feedback_new success returns absolute Path (leaks EKA_HOME location to MCP client). This is intentional per CLI behavior and scoped to caller; not a cross-boundary leak. Store Save/Chmod ensures 0700/0600, MarkPublished uses atomic write .tmp + Rename, timeout 60s context + 10s dial/TLS + 30s header. Long title slug not length-capped (OS will error \u003e255 -\u003e sanitized \u003cpath\u003e) — low DoS risk bounded by 64 MiB line cap at MCP Serve. No action required; optionally cap slug/title to 80 chars for UX.","Assumptions: EKA_HOME isolation per test (t.TempDir + t.Setenv), pack.Version and runtime.GOOS/GOARCH injection trusted, GitHub API surface stable, MCP client respects isError semantics (tool errors != JSON-RPC errors). No E2E live network test executed (httptest covers).","Recommendation: approve. Next steps: (1) optionally fix implementation note cmt:mcp-feedback-tool-implementation (populate summary/changes/tests) and re-validate draft list to clear invalid marker — not blocking publish; (2) keep token ldflags practice unchanged; (3) no code rework for feedback tools. Note deviation documented here satisfies review trail."],"role":"review","verdict":"approve"}